  "summary_en": "Transport Canada's updated framework describes the federal approach to connected and automated vehicle safety. It covers the Motor Vehicle Safety Act self-certification regime, exemptions for innovation, non-binding testing, safety assessment and cybersecurity guidance, public awareness work, international harmonization (UNECE WP.29/WP.1), research and funding programs.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Self-certification regime under the Motor Vehicle Safety Act with Canada Motor Vehicle Safety Standards and oversight program",
   "Ministerial exemption authority (up to five years) to enable testing and innovation",
   "Non-binding guidance: Testing ADS Guidelines v2.0, Safety Assessment for ADS, Vehicle Cyber Security Guidance",
   "Alignment with the US and UNECE WP.29/WP.1 for harmonized regulations",
   "Research on simulation and scenario-based validation toward future regulation; funding programs"
  ],
